# /clear

Description:
  Clear all context and start fresh for next task. Use when transitioning
  between distinct tasks to prevent context pollution.

Usage:
  /clear
  /clear --save-state
  /clear --archive

Options:
  --save-state   Save current state before clearing
  --archive      Archive current context to history

Behavior:
  1. If --save-state: persist current task state
  2. If --archive: move context to history log
  3. Clear all working memory
  4. Reset to minimal context (INDEX.sdd only)
  5. Ready for next task

Output:
  [tokens: cleared]
  [state: fresh]
  [history: archived|discarded]

State: +
